On Friday 05 September 2008 4:28:58 pm you wrote:
> At Fri, 5 Sep 2008 02:46:50 +1000,
>
> Travis Place wrote:
> > Hello everyone,
> >
> > Im Travis (wishie) once of the many helpers who man the unofficial #alsa
> > on freenode irc network.. I usually spend my time fixing other peoples
> > sound issues, but now i have my own.
> >
> > I have a HP DV2839TX laptop, and i get ALOT of static when recording via
> > the inbuilt mic. Also, the mic controls are very strange.. I have (in the
> > Capture section of alsamixer).. Digital, Docking Mic, External Mic,
> > Internal Mic.. only the "Digital" control seems to effect my recording
> > volume at all.
>
> The "Digital Capture Volume" is alsa-lib softvol plugin element, and
> works globally.  In the case of a digital mic (i.e. usually without a
> volume control), sometimes this is the only effective control.
>
> > Strangely, though, the '* Mic' controls in the PLAYBACK section of
> > alsamixer do change the recording properties somewhat (volume being the
> > main factor).
>
> If you mean about "Mic Boost" or such, then it's a known
> (long-standing) bug in ALSA mixer interface.  This appears twice, for
> playback and capture, but only the playback one works.
There is no "Mic Boost" that i can see in either section of alsamixer. There 
are only the "Docking/External/Internal Mic" controls. Which, in the CAPTURE 
section of alsamixer, do nothing. In the PLAYBACK section, the 'External Mic' 
control seems to adjust gain/volume. But im using the INTERNAL mic that this 
laptop has. So something very strange is going on.

>
> > In any event, i get a rather large amount of static, no matter what mixer
> > settings i try. This isnt a problem in the 'other' OS.
> >
> > My alsa-info.sh output for alsa-driver 1.0.16 is at :
